        "title": "Old Reddit a threat to AI data scraping, says platform, with changes coming",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/06/old-reddit-a-threat-to-ai-data-scraping-says-platform-with-changes-coming/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Old-Reddit-a-threat-to-AI-data-scraping-says-platform-with-changes-coming.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When Reddit significantly changed its user interface way back in 2018, there were widespread protests from those who preferred the original. The company has retained access to this at <a href=\"https://old.reddit.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">old.reddit.com</a>, and last year promised this version would continue to exist for as long as people kept using it.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That promise may now be under some degree of threat as Reddit says that it “plans to make changes” to Old Reddit in order to protect against AI data scraping … </p>",
        "type": "Technology",
        "source": "9to5Mac"
