        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/06/apple-releases-security-updates-to-macos-tahoe-sequoia-and-sonoma/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/update.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Update, 2:24 p.m. ET: </strong>Apple has now revealed that the updates address a Screen Sharing vulnerability. You can learn more about it <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/06/apples-latest-macos-updates-address-a-serious-screen-sharing-vulnerability/\">here</a>. The original story follows below.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple rolled out macOS Sonoma 14.8.9, macOS Sequoia 15.7.9, and macOS Tahoe 26.6.1 today, skipping developer and public betas altogether. Here are the details.</p>",
        "type": "Technology",
